{"root_text": {"uid": "snp2.4", "lang": "en", "is_root": false, "title": "The Discourse on the Blessings", "author": "Bhikkhu Ānandajoti", "author_short": "Ānandajoti", "author_uid": "anandajoti", "next": {"author_uid": "mills", "lang": "en", "name": "Spiky the Native Spirit ", "uid": "snp2.5"}, "previous": {"author_uid": "mills", "lang": "en", "name": "Conscience ", "uid": "snp2.3"}, "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset='UTF-8'>\n<meta name='author' content='Bhikkhu Ānandajoti'>\n<title></title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<article id='snp2.4' lang='en'>\n<header>\n<h1 class='sutta'>2.4. The Discourse on the Blessings</h1>\n</header>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc1' href='#sc1'>SC 1</a><span class='evam'>This is what I heard</span>: At one time the Gracious One was dwelling near Sāvatthi, at Anāthapiṇḍika’s grounds in Jeta’s Wood. Then a certain god, at the end of the night, having lit up the whole of Jeta’s Wood with his surpassing beauty, approached the Gracious One, and after approaching and worshipping the Gracious One, he stood on one side. While standing on one side that god recited this verse to the Gracious One:</p>\n<blockquote class='gatha'>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc2' href='#sc2'>SC 2</a>“Many are the gods and the men<br>\nwho have thought about the blessings<br>\nhoping for safety:<br>\nnow please say what is a supreme blessing.”</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc3' href='#sc3'>SC 3</a>“Not associating with fools,<br>\nwith the wise associating,<br>\nhonouring those worthy of honour:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc4' href='#sc4'>SC 4</a>“Living in a suitable place,<br>\nformerly having done good deeds,<br>\nhaving the right aspiration for oneself:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc5' href='#sc5'>SC 5</a>“Having great learning and craft,<br>\nbeing disciplined and well trained,<br>\nand whatever words are well spoken:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc6' href='#sc6'>SC 6</a>“Attending on one’s mother and father,<br>\nlooking after one’s wife and sons,<br>\nhaving work that is not confusing:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc7' href='#sc7'>SC 7</a>“Giving, and living by the Dhamma,<br>\nand looking after one’s relatives,<br>\n<span class='add'>performing</span> actions that are blameless:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc8' href='#sc8'>SC 8</a>“Abstaining, refraining from bad deeds,<br>\nrestraint from intoxicating drink,<br>\nbeing heedful regarding <span class='add'>all</span> things:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc9' href='#sc9'>SC 9</a>“Having respect and being humble,<br>\nbeing satisfied and grateful,<br>\nlistening to the Dhamma at the right time:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc10' href='#sc10'>SC 10</a>“Being patient and easily spoken to,<br>\nhaving sight of ascetics,<br>\ndiscussing the Dhamma at the right time:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc11' href='#sc11'>SC 11</a>“Austerity, living spiritually,<br>\ninsight into the noble truths,<br>\nand experiencing Emancipation:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc12' href='#sc12'>SC 12</a>“He whose mind does not waver,<br>\nwhen it is touched by things of this world,<br>\nbeing griefless, dustless, and secure:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc13' href='#sc13'>SC 13</a>“Having done as here directed,<br>\nbeing undefeated everywhere,<br>\nthey go everywhere in safety:<br>\nfor them this is a supreme blessing.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'>The Discourse on the Blessings is Finished</p>\n<footer>\n<p>Translated by Bhikkhu <span class='author'>Ānandajoti</span>.</p>\n<p>The text and translation, together with detailed notes and discussions, may be found in multiple formats on the translator’s website, <a href='http://www.ancient-buddhist-texts.net/Texts-and-Translations/Khuddakapatha/Khuddakapatha.htm'>Ancient Buddhist Texts</a>.</p>\n<p>Used by kind permission of Bhikkhu Ānandajoti.</p>\n<p>The original translation was released under the following licence: <a href='http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en_US'>Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License</a>.</p>\n<p>Prepared for SuttaCentral by <span class='editor'>Bhikkhu Sujato</span>.</p>\n</footer>\n</article>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}, "translation": {"uid": "snp2.4", "lang": "en", "is_root": false, "title": "The Discourse on the Blessings", "author": "Bhikkhu Ānandajoti", "author_short": "Ānandajoti", "author_uid": "anandajoti", "next": {"author_uid": "mills", "lang": "en", "name": "Spiky the Native Spirit ", "uid": "snp2.5"}, "previous": {"author_uid": "mills", "lang": "en", "name": "Conscience ", "uid": "snp2.3"}, "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset='UTF-8'>\n<meta name='author' content='Bhikkhu Ānandajoti'>\n<title></title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<article id='snp2.4' lang='en'>\n<header>\n<h1 class='sutta'>2.4. The Discourse on the Blessings</h1>\n</header>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc1' href='#sc1'>SC 1</a><span class='evam'>This is what I heard</span>: At one time the Gracious One was dwelling near Sāvatthi, at Anāthapiṇḍika’s grounds in Jeta’s Wood. Then a certain god, at the end of the night, having lit up the whole of Jeta’s Wood with his surpassing beauty, approached the Gracious One, and after approaching and worshipping the Gracious One, he stood on one side. While standing on one side that god recited this verse to the Gracious One:</p>\n<blockquote class='gatha'>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc2' href='#sc2'>SC 2</a>“Many are the gods and the men<br>\nwho have thought about the blessings<br>\nhoping for safety:<br>\nnow please say what is a supreme blessing.”</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc3' href='#sc3'>SC 3</a>“Not associating with fools,<br>\nwith the wise associating,<br>\nhonouring those worthy of honour:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc4' href='#sc4'>SC 4</a>“Living in a suitable place,<br>\nformerly having done good deeds,<br>\nhaving the right aspiration for oneself:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc5' href='#sc5'>SC 5</a>“Having great learning and craft,<br>\nbeing disciplined and well trained,<br>\nand whatever words are well spoken:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc6' href='#sc6'>SC 6</a>“Attending on one’s mother and father,<br>\nlooking after one’s wife and sons,<br>\nhaving work that is not confusing:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc7' href='#sc7'>SC 7</a>“Giving, and living by the Dhamma,<br>\nand looking after one’s relatives,<br>\n<span class='add'>performing</span> actions that are blameless:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc8' href='#sc8'>SC 8</a>“Abstaining, refraining from bad deeds,<br>\nrestraint from intoxicating drink,<br>\nbeing heedful regarding <span class='add'>all</span> things:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc9' href='#sc9'>SC 9</a>“Having respect and being humble,<br>\nbeing satisfied and grateful,<br>\nlistening to the Dhamma at the right time:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc10' href='#sc10'>SC 10</a>“Being patient and easily spoken to,<br>\nhaving sight of ascetics,<br>\ndiscussing the Dhamma at the right time:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc11' href='#sc11'>SC 11</a>“Austerity, living spiritually,<br>\ninsight into the noble truths,<br>\nand experiencing Emancipation:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc12' href='#sc12'>SC 12</a>“He whose mind does not waver,<br>\nwhen it is touched by things of this world,<br>\nbeing griefless, dustless, and secure:<br>\nthis is a supreme blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc13' href='#sc13'>SC 13</a>“Having done as here directed,<br>\nbeing undefeated everywhere,<br>\nthey go everywhere in safety:<br>\nfor them this is a supreme blessing.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'>The Discourse on the Blessings is Finished</p>\n<footer>\n<p>Translated by Bhikkhu <span class='author'>Ānandajoti</span>.</p>\n<p>The text and translation, together with detailed notes and discussions, may be found in multiple formats on the translator’s website, <a href='http://www.ancient-buddhist-texts.net/Texts-and-Translations/Khuddakapatha/Khuddakapatha.htm'>Ancient Buddhist Texts</a>.</p>\n<p>Used by kind permission of Bhikkhu Ānandajoti.</p>\n<p>The original translation was released under the following licence: <a href='http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en_US'>Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License</a>.</p>\n<p>Prepared for SuttaCentral by <span class='editor'>Bhikkhu Sujato</span>.</p>\n</footer>\n</article>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}, "segmented": false, "suttaplex": {"acronym": "Snp 2.4", "alt_acronym": null, "volpages": "PTS Snp 46, PTS 47", "alt_volpages": null, "uid": "snp2.4", "blurb": "A list of the types of skillful behavior that give blessings and protection.", "difficulty": null, "original_title": "Maṅgalasutta", "root_lang": "pli", "root_lang_name": "Pāli", "type": "leaf", "from": null, "translated_title": "True Blessings ", "translations": [{"lang": "de", "lang_name": "Deutsch", "is_root": false, "author": "Sabbamitta", "author_short": "sabbamitta", "author_uid": "sabbamitta", "publication_date": "2019", "id": "snp2.4_translation-de-sabbamitta", "segmented": true, "title": "Segen ", "volpage": null, "has_comment": false}, {"lang": "en", "lang_name": "English", "is_root": false, "author": "Bhikkhu Sujato", "author_short": "sujato", "author_uid": "sujato", "publication_date": "2018", "id": "snp2.4_translation-en-sujato", "segmented": true, "title": "True Blessings ", "volpage": null, "has_comment": false}, {"lang": "lt", 